  "fullDescription": "Bring festive holiday charm to your tabletop with this Christmas Tree Candy Bowl 3D STL. This decorative Christmas design combines a beautifully layered evergreen tree topper with a detailed candy bowl, creating a unique seasonal centerpiece for displaying sweets, treats, ornaments, or small decorative items.\n\nThe model features a golden star topper, layered green Christmas tree branches, red bows, shiny red ornaments, golden bead garlands, holly accents, and a richly decorated red-and-gold bowl with snowflake details.\n\nFeatures\nChristmas tree and bowl combination design\nLarge decorative golden star topper\nLayered evergreen tree branches\nMultiple festive red bows\nDecorative red Christmas ornaments\nGolden bead garland details\nHolly and berry accents\nRed-and-gold ornamental bowl\nSnowflake decorative details\nStable decorative base\nLarge open bowl for displaying treats or small items\nPremium festive tabletop appearance\nIdeal For\nChristmas candy bowl\nHoliday tabletop décor\nChristmas centerpiece\nSweet and treat display\nChristmas party decoration\nMantel decoration\nShelf decoration\nHoliday home décor\nFestive gift collections\nSeasonal 3D printing projects\nPrinting & Technical Recommendations\nFile Format: STL\nCompatibility: FDM and Resin 3D printers\nFilament Suggestion: PLA, Silk PLA, Matte PLA, PETG, or compatible resin\nSupports: Light supports may be required around the tree branches, bows, and decorative overhangs depending on orientation\nScaling: Easily scalable for different display and bowl sizes\nPrint Orientation: Keep the model upright on its integrated base\nInfill: Moderate infill is recommended for a stable decorative model\nFinishing: Multi-color filament or post-print painting can be used to emphasize the Christmas colors and decorative details\n\nPlease Note: This is a digital 3D model file. No physical product will be shipped. Please check your 3D printer and slicing software compatibility before printing. This 3D model is available only in STL color — if you’d like it colored, you’ll need to open the STL file in separate software to color it yourself.",
